  array['family-owned', 'generations-old', 'neighborhood-institution']::public.story_tag[], $tt$A two-day mole, a recipe tin by the register, and three generations who still cook the way the first one did.$tt$, 'both',
  $tt$Mole rojo with handmade tortillas$tt$, $tt$It is the dish the whole restaurant grew from, and it tastes like the family's patience: two days of work in every spoonful.$tt$, array[$tt$Whose handwriting is on the oldest recipe card?$tt$, $tt$What was on the very first plate you ever served?$tt$, $tt$Which part of the mole do you refuse to rush?$tt$, $tt$What do regulars still ask for that is not on the menu?$tt$]::text[],
